WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.441
Lia: Hi everyone!

2
00:00:01.741 --> 00:00:06.321
I’m Lia and welcome to my vlog about hip-hop dance, my favourite hobby.

3
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.403
Lia: Today I’m at the dance studio.

4
00:00:09.703 --> 00:00:12.968
It’s cloudy and windy outside, but it’s really hot in here.

5
00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:16.677
I’m wearing baggy trousers, a hoodie and my old trainers.

6
00:00:16.977 --> 00:00:22.435
Right now my group is practising the new routine and our teacher is filming us to check the moves.

7
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.191
Lia: I usually dance on Wednesdays at six o’clock for one hour.

8
00:00:27.491 --> 00:00:34.915
But this month I’m rehearsing three times a week, because our Christmas show is on the nineteenth of December and we want to be ready.

9
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.027
Lia: Did you know?

10
00:00:37.327 --> 00:00:46.244
Hip-hop was born in New York in the nineteen-seventies, at street parties in the Bronx, and breaking was at the Paris Olympics in twenty twenty-four.

11
00:00:46.544 --> 00:00:50.824
I think that’s amazing, because it started on the street and now it’s a sport.

12
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:59.413
Lia: I love dancing to music I know, and I prefer group routines to solos, because you feel the energy of the others.

13
00:00:59.713 --> 00:01:03.866
I hate forgetting a move on stage, but I believe mistakes help you learn.

14
00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.501
Lia: Here are my three tips.

15
00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:10.206
Set a time limit, because one hour of videos is enough.

16
00:01:10.506 --> 00:01:14.243
Turn off notifications when you practise, so you can concentrate.

17
00:01:14.543 --> 00:01:18.279
And keep your phone out of your bedroom, because the light keeps you awake.

18
00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:22.141
That’s the one I’m going to apply: my phone sleeps in the kitchen.

19
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.012
Lia: Photos: me, Nadia’s sister and Urban Steps studio.

20
00:01:27.312 --> 00:01:35.322
Facts: “Hip-hop”, Encyclopedia website, 2026, and “Breaking”, Olympics website, 2024.

21
00:01:35.622 --> 00:01:36.853
Thanks for watching!

22
00:01:37.153 --> 00:01:38.256
See you next time!
